{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>El who brought him out of Egypt.</b> Who causes this greatness for them? El, who brings them out of Egypt with His strength and His loftiness — He will consume the nations that are His foes." "<b>And their bones.</b> Of the foes." "<b>He will gnaw.</b> Menachem explained it as a term of breaking, and so ״לֹא גָרְמוּ לַבֹּקֶר״ (Zephaniah 3), and so ״וְאֶת חֲרָשֶׂיהָ תְּגָרֵמִי״ (Ezekiel 23). And I say it is a term of bone — that he gnaws the flesh with his teeth from all around, and the marrow inside, and leaves the bone standing in its bareness." "<b>And his half he will shatter.</b> Onkelos rendered: half of the foes — their portion, as in (Genesis 49) ״בַּעֲלֵי חִצִּים״ — masters of palguta. And so יִמְחָץ is a term as in ״וּמָחֲצָה וְחָלְפָה רַקָּתוֹ״ (Judges 5) — that they will split their land. And it can also be explained literally as arrows — the arrows of the Holy One, blessed be He, he will dash in the blood of the foes, dip and plunge in blood, as in ״לְמַעַן תִּמְחַץ רַגְלְךָ בְּדָם״ (Psalms 68); and it does not depart from the sense of striking, as in ״מָחַצְתִּי״ (Deuteronomy 32) — for what is dyed in blood appears as though dashed and stricken."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:37.447566002Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}